    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0547" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/2741: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Casablanca</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Casablanca</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-15T16:00:00+01:00">January 15, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. My 18, January 14, 4 p.m. French and British have also cancelled permissions
                    their troops. Belief among middle class Arabs and workers is that Nationalist
                    movement is supported and backed by United States Government. Consulate
                    considers this belief encouraged by ill-considered actions of officers mentioned
                    in my despatch 1186 November 22<anchor n="42" xml:id="d573-f1"/> and by over
                    friendly attitude of former U.S. general officers here. French are taking
                    precautions but do not intend to interfere unless native demonstrations become
                    disorderly.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Algiers as my 5, to Tangier as 6 and true reading to Rabat.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
